G5 -- can a z-dependent gas mis-scaling ALONE produce the pattern?  g_bar,analysis = g_bar,true x 10^(beta log10((1 + z)/2.5))
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] C4 machinery: the flat-truth mock at beta = 0 gives slopes (0, expected) equal to the baseline expectations to 1e-9
         +4.38e-17, -0.039691 vs -0.039691
  M1 (flat truth): the mis-scaling that reproduces the observed delta_flat slope +0.171: beta = -1.254 -> differential dlog M_bar (z 0.6 -> 2.5) = -0.426 dex; the rival's slope there +0.122 (observed +0.108)
  M2 (rival truth): best beta = -0.916 (dlog M_bar = -0.312 dex) with chi2 = 0.00 (slopes +0.171, +0.108 vs observed +0.171, +0.108); within the plausible range |dlog M_bar| <= 0.2 dex (|beta| <= 0.59): best chi2 = 10.00 at beta = -0.58; at beta = 0: chi2 = 75.8
  -> M2 produces the pattern at a plausible mis-scaling (chi2 < 2 with |dlog M_bar| <= 0.2 dex): no; the stress variant V1 (gas fraction fixed with z) corresponds to about -0.18 dex of differential M_bar

